{
  "_comment": "Allowlist for scripts/check-dump.py. tables: every table and column order the Worker's migrations create (a test keeps this equal to them) plus Cloudflare's own bookkeeping tables. A new table or column needs a reviewed edit here. hex_ids: columns that hold an opaque 32-hex id or keyed hash. numeric: every numeric column (and the text columns that hold a counter or a timestamp) with the kind of value it may hold; numeric_kinds gives the allowed inclusive ranges (small stays under 2^24 and ms is epoch milliseconds from 2020 to 2099, so no value can be a 32-bit address). A numeric value outside its range fails. patterns: a regex a value in that column (any table) must fully match. spaces_ok: column names (any table) whose values may hold spaces (place names, and a migration's applied_at timestamp). digit_tokens_ok / hex_tokens_ok: columns (table.column) allowed to hold a long digit run (hour counters, timestamps, an email local part) / any 8-character hex token; every other text column refuses an 8-character all-hex token and a run of 9 or more digits. optional_tables: tables a Cloudflare export may leave out. A numeric value in a column with no numeric rule is always an error. bare_number_ok: columns that may hold a digits-only name (an email local part) as long as it is below 2^24; larger digit runs and every dotted, octal or hex form are read as addresses there too.",
